Lunite is free to download and use. Sections 3 to 6 say at more length what the app shows the first time it starts; sections 1, 2 and 7 to 9 add what that screen leaves out. By using Lunite you agree to all of them.

1. WHAT YOU MAY DO
   You may download Lunite from its official release page and run it on your own PCs.

2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO
   You may not redistribute, sell, rehost, modify, decompile or reverse engineer Lunite, or remove its notices, without written permission - except where the law in your country allows it anyway.

3. WHAT LUNITE DOES
   The check-up only reads. It changes no settings on your PC; it saves only its own files, like its results and report cards. No setting on your PC changes without your yes: every fix has its own tick box, and only what you approve runs. Each fix you apply keeps its own UNDO in WHAT CHANGED - if the setting has moved on since, or Lunite could not save its undo record, it says so instead. The sign-in popup switch in SETTINGS is not a fix: you turn it back off with its own button there. Removals in the removal room cannot be undone, and the room says so before you agree. This section describes how Lunite is designed to work. It is not a warranty, and sections 4 and 5 apply to it.

4. NO WARRANTY
   Lunite is provided "as is" and "as available", without any warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose or non-infringement. It cannot promise any particular result on your PC.

5. LIMIT OF LIABILITY
   As far as the law allows, Lunite's maker is not liable for any loss or damage from using Lunite or from not being able to use it - including lost data, lost profits, or damage to hardware or software. Any liability that cannot be excluded is limited to what you paid for Lunite. Some places do not allow these exclusions or limits, so they may not all apply to you.

6. NAMES OF OTHER PRODUCTS
   Product and company names Lunite shows - in the check-up, the hardware view and the removal room - belong to their owners. Lunite is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by any of them. They are named only to identify the product on your PC.

7. SENDING A REPORT
   A report leaves your PC only when you press SEND on the SEND A REPORT screen. A report you send is saved in Lunite's Google account (its Google Drive and its inbox, luniteapp@gmail.com) and stays there until it is deleted. To have a report you sent deleted, email luniteapp@gmail.com and quote its tag.

8. CHANGES TO THESE TERMS
   If these terms change, the new version is shown in the app the next time it starts, and published with the release that brings it.

